# SpringCoat Usage

This covers SquirrelJME SpringCoat, for general usage see [Usage](usage.mkd).

## Common Issues

***SpringCoat is too slow for my system:*** SpringCoat is a pure interpreter
focused on compatibility that is implemented on top of an existing Java
Virtual Machine. Due to such, it has no built-in optimization strategies,
therefor it is recommended you use `-Xemulator:nanocoat`. If you are on
standalone you additionally have the option of `-Xemulator:hosted` with
no regard to accuracy and compatibility.
